  "aiContextParagraph": "Jensen Huang, who resigned as CEO of Nvidia in November 2026, has indicated a willingness to resume his leadership role if sought by the company's board of directors. His departure followed reports of personal controversies that prompted significant scrutiny from United States lawmakers. Following his resignation, Colette Kress was appointed as the firm's interim leader. Congressional interest remains high, with the Senate requesting testimony from both Huang and other figures regarding the situation. Reports indicate that the Nvidia board is not currently considering his reinstatement. The discourse surrounding his potential return is fueled by a petition signed by 190,000 people. Huang is now set to appear before Congress for closed-door questioning on December 1, a development that follows threats of a subpoena regarding an ongoing investigation into the circumstances of his departure.",
